<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xsd:schema xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema"
	targetNamespace="http://ei/core/businessinformation">
	<xsd:element name="BusinessInformation">
		<xsd:complexType>
			<xsd:annotation><xsd:documentation>
This business object contains classification and identification information about an organization doing business with Chubb.
			</xsd:documentation></xsd:annotation>
			<xsd:sequence>
				<xsd:element name="SICCode" type="xsd:string"
					minOccurs="0">
					<xsd:annotation><xsd:documentation>
This element identifies a major industry classification as determined by the US Federal Government. 
The first two characters of the SIC code are the Major Group.
The last two characters of the SIC code are the Industry Code.  
The E1T00331 Corporate Table contains valid values for the SIC Code, as well as columns for Major Group and Industry Code. 
The E1T00321 Corporate Table contains valid values for only the Major Group.
					</xsd:documentation></xsd:annotation>
				</xsd:element>
				<xsd:element name="NAICSCode" type="xsd:string"
					minOccurs="0">
					<xsd:annotation><xsd:documentation>
This element identifies a category of business as defined by the United States, Mexican, and Canadian governments. 
The E1T00611 Corporate Table contains valid values this element. 
				</xsd:documentation></xsd:annotation>
				</xsd:element>
				<xsd:element name="NotforProfitIndicator"
					type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0">
					<xsd:annotation><xsd:documentation>
This element specifies whether a company is organized for a purpose other than the generation of profit.  
Valid options for this element are 'Y' or 'N'.
					</xsd:documentation></xsd:annotation>
				</xsd:element>
				<xsd:element name="MultinationalIndicator"
					type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0">
					<xsd:annotation><xsd:documentation>
This element specifies whether a company has businesses in more than one country.  
Valid options for this element are 'Y' or 'N'. 
					</xsd:documentation></xsd:annotation>
				</xsd:element>
				<xsd:element name="TaxPayerIdNumber" type="xsd:string"
					minOccurs="0">
					<xsd:annotation><xsd:documentation>This element is an identification number assigned by the U.S. government to identify a legal entity that has employees.  This is also known as EIN.
					</xsd:documentation></xsd:annotation>
				</xsd:element>
				<xsd:element name="EnterpriseOwnership"
					type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0">
					<xsd:annotation><xsd:documentation>
This element describes the regulatory system under which a  company is organized and operated (e.g. PUBLIC, PRIVATE, NON-PROFIT).
The E1T00291 Corporate Table contains valid values for this element. 
					</xsd:documentation></xsd:annotation>
				</xsd:element>
				<xsd:element name="GovtOwnedIndicator" type="xsd:string"
					minOccurs="0">
					<xsd:annotation><xsd:documentation>
This element indicates whether a legal entity is owned by the government.  
Valid options for this element are 'Y' or 'N'.
					</xsd:documentation></xsd:annotation>
				</xsd:element>
				<xsd:element name="InitialYearwithChubb"
					type="xsd:string" minOccurs="0">
					<xsd:annotation><xsd:documentation>
This element is the first year an Insured begins a business relationship with Chubb.
					</xsd:documentation></xsd:annotation>
				</xsd:element>
				<xsd:element name="AccountReviewDate" type="xsd:date"
					minOccurs="0">
					<xsd:annotation><xsd:documentation>
This element identifies when an an account needs to be reviewed. 
					</xsd:documentation></xsd:annotation>
				</xsd:element>
				<xsd:element name="EstablishedYear" type="xsd:string"
					minOccurs="0">
					<xsd:annotation><xsd:documentation>
This element identifies the year a business was established.
					</xsd:documentation></xsd:annotation>
				</xsd:element>
				<xsd:element name="DFIAccountCode" type="xsd:string"
					minOccurs="0">
					<xsd:annotation><xsd:documentation>
This element used to identify specific types of business underwritten by DFI. 
This element is also known as Policy Account Identification Code.
The E1T00071 Corporate Table contains valid values for this element. 
					</xsd:documentation></xsd:annotation>
				</xsd:element>
			</xsd:sequence>
		</xsd:complexType>
	</xsd:element>
</xsd:schema>
